  "title": " ForrestGump-MEG",
  "description": "ForrestGump-MEG is a magnetoencephalography dataset recorded from 11 participants while they watched the roughly 2-hour Chinese-dubbed audio-visual movie Forrest Gump. Data were acquired with a 275-channel CTF MEG system and are accompanied by T1-weighted anatomical MRI. Derivatives include preprocessed MEG (bad channel removal, high-pass filtering, ICA artifact removal), fMRIPrep-processed anatomical data, FreeSurfer surfaces, and MEG-MRI coregistration files. The authors acknowledge the studyforrest project (OpenNeuro ds000113) for its contribution.",
  "methods_description": "MEG was recorded with a 275-channel CTF system while participants watched the Chinese-dubbed Forrest Gump movie. T1w images were processed with the fMRIPrep anatomical pipeline. MEG data were preprocessed with MNE: bad channel detection and removal, 1 Hz high-pass filtering, and ICA-based artifact removal. Data are organized in MEG-BIDS using MNE-BIDS.",
